From: Claude (CT108) <claude@ct108>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: boot the VPU at EL2 like Windows' QcSkExt

At EL2 (no Hyper-V) TZ authenticates the Iris firmware (PAS 9) but does
not handle MEM_PROTECT_VIDEO_VAR or SET_REMOTE_STATE: on Windows the CSRT
(QCOM group, policy 2) routes them to QcSkExt8380 in VTL1, which programs
the VPU windows and releases its reset. Do the same from the driver:

- own "video-firmware" context bank, firmware loaded with
  qcom_mdt_pas_load + IOMMU mapping at 0 (context bank port and Secure
  PAS from the list);
- iris_el2_vpu_boot(): FW/CPA/non-pixel windows, SEC_SID, fuses via
  SMC 0x2000802 and the VPU CPU taken out of reset;
- set_hw_state: suspend does nothing and resume repeats the boot.

Tested 24/25-10-2026 on a Surface Pro 11 (x1e80100) at EL2: H.264, HEVC
and VP9 identical to software decoding frame by frame; AV1 149/150
frames (the first one is lost); 8 h of s2idle with the driver loaded.

